---
import Navigation from "../../components/navigation.astro";
import { posts } from "../../data/posts.js";

const post = posts.find((post) => post.slug === "post_fifteen");

if (!post) {
  throw new Error("Post not found: post_fifteen");
}

const { title, date, dateTime, tags } = post;
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>{title} | Ivy Duncan</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A review of Regas, a fantasy romance BL manhwa."
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <Navigation />

    <main>
      <article class="blog-post">
        <div class="container narrow">
          <a href="/blog" class="back-link">← Back to Blog</a>

          <header class="post-header">
            <p class="post-date">
              <time datetime={dateTime}>{date}</time>
            </p>

            <h1>{title}</h1>

            <div class="post-tags">
              {tags.map((tag) => (
                <a
                  href={`/blog/tag/${tag.toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, "-")}`}
                  class="post-tag"
                >
                  {tag}
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </header>

          <div class="post-content">
            <p class="review-intro">
              A quick review of <em>Regas</em>.
            </p>

            <figure class="cover-image">
              <img
                src="/images/blog/manhwa_review_one.jpg"
                alt="Cover of Regas manhwa"
              />
            </figure>

            <div class="review-details">
              <p><strong>Rating:</strong> 5/5 stars</p>
              <p><strong>Where to Read:</strong> Tapas</p>
              <p>
                <strong>How I Heard About It:</strong> TikTok
              </p>
            </div>

            <h2>The Plot</h2>

            <p>
              In this world, kings have the powers of dragons. These powers
              make them stronger, but they also make them more aggressive and
              difficult to manage. Their partners, called Regas, help calm
              their dragon urges.
            </p>

            <p>
              The story follows a king and his Regas as they struggle against
              the royal council, which has been poisoning generations of
              kings.
            </p>

            <h2>My Thoughts</h2>

            <p>
              I absolutely loved this story! It made me laugh, the art is
              beautiful, and the villains are really intriguing. The pacing is
              also great. The manhwa is getting close to the end, and I'm
              excited to see how everything wraps up.
            </p>

            <p>
              The original web novel has sex scenes, but the manhwa is rated
              R15, so those scenes won't be adapted. There is occasionally
              some kissing, though. I usually prefer my manhwa to be a little
              spicier, but the plot is good enough that I don't mind.
            </p>

            <p>
              Overall, this is a five-star read for me. If you enjoy fantasy,
              romance, beautiful artwork, and political intrigue, I definitely
              recommend giving it a try!
            </p>

            <p><strong>SPOILERS BEYOND THIS POINT</strong></p>

            <h2>Spoilers</h2>

            <p>
              One thing I have mixed feelings about is the relationship
              between the main characters and how it develops.
            </p>

            <p>
              Regas first meets the king when the prince is only eight years
              old, while Regas is eighteen. Regas becomes the prince's
              caretaker for a few months, but the royal council eventually
              conspires to assassinate him.
            </p>

            <p>
              Years later, the prince is now a twenty-year-old king, and
              Regas reincarnates in the body of a very pretty man who is
              around the king's age. Their romantic relationship only begins
              at this point.
            </p>

            <p>
              I understand that Regas is now in a different body and that
              their romance doesn't begin until they're both adults. Still,
              I find the situation a little weird because Regas knew the king
              when he was a child. Regas occasionally thinks of the king in a
              childlike way, which makes it harder for me to fully get behind
              their relationship.
            </p>

            <p>
              That said, I still really enjoy the story, and it hasn't
              changed how much I love the overall plot. It's just one aspect
              of the romance that leaves me feeling a little conflicted.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="post-footer">
            <a href="/blog" class="back-link">← Back to Blog</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="container">
        <p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Ivy Duncan. All rights reserved.</p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .container {
    width: min(1100px, calc(100% - 3rem));
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .blog-post {
    padding: 5rem 0 7rem;
    background: #fffaf4;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: #765f48;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .post-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #c9c2b8;
  }

  .post-date {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: #765f48;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .post-header h1 {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    color: #3f3a35;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .post-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .post-tag {
    color: #765f48;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .post-tag:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .post-content {
    color: #3f3a35;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .post-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .post-content h2 {
    margin: 3rem 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .review-intro {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .cover-image {
    margin: 2rem auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cover-image img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 300px;
    height: auto;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .review-details {
    margin: 2rem 0 3rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
    background: #f4efe7;
  }

  .review-details p {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .review-details p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .post-footer {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #c9c2b8;
  }

  .post-footer .back-link {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .site-footer {
    padding: 2rem 0;
    background: #f4efe7;
  }

  .site-footer p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #765f48;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .container {
      width: min(100% - 2rem, 1100px);
    }

    .blog-post {
      padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
    }

    .post-header {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .review-details {
      padding: 1.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>